# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# The receive-activity counter, shared by the two indicators that encode "how
# much is this dongle hearing" - the mono led0 heartbeat (Kconfig.heartbeat_led)
# and the NeoPixel hue wheel (Kconfig.rgb_led). Both `select` the symbol below;
# neither owns it.
#
# IT USED TO LIVE IN Kconfig.rgb_led, and moving it is the whole reason this
# file exists. The count is one atomic increment in antr_on_message(), and a
# second indicator that wanted it had a choice between adding a THIRD hook to
# the bridge's hot path or generalising the second. ant_activity.h carries the
# argument, unchanged from where it was written, for why the second hook could
# not reuse CONFIG_ANT_DONGLE_RX_TAP (link-time
# resolution, one definition per image, already owned by
# apps/dongle_thread/src/rx_tap.c); a third would have had no such argument.
#
# rsourced by apps/dongle/Kconfig, apps/dongle_thread/Kconfig and
# apps/dongle_ti/Kconfig - every application that compiles the serial bridge.
# `select` on a symbol that is not visible in the tree is a Kconfig error, so it
# has to be in scope wherever either indicator is.

config ANT_DONGLE_ACTIVITY_CLAIMED
	bool
	help
	  Set by the indicator that has taken the counter, so a second one can
	  depend on it being clear. Not user-selectable.

	  ONE READER PER IMAGE IS A HARD RULE, not a preference:
	  ant_activity.h's consumers drain with atomic_clear(), so two of them
	  would each get about half the traffic and both would show a quiet
	  room - an indicator that is confidently wrong, which is worse than one
	  that is absent. Today CONFIG_ANT_DONGLE_RGB_LED claims it and
	  CONFIG_ANT_DONGLE_HEARTBEAT_LED_ACTIVITY yields, which is what the
	  shipping Feather row builds: NeoPixel showing the rate, mono led0 on
	  its fixed flash.

	  IT EXISTS RATHER THAN A PLAIN `depends on !ANT_DONGLE_RGB_LED` because
	  that symbol is defined only where Kconfig.rgb_led is rsourced - one
	  application out of three - and a dependency naming a symbol that does
	  not exist in two of the trees is a dependency that reads as deliberate
	  and evaluates to nothing. This symbol is defined wherever the counter
	  is, which is wherever either indicator can be.

config ANT_DONGLE_ACTIVITY_COUNT
	bool
	help
	  Compile apps/common/ant_activity.c and make ant_activity_note_msg()
	  real. Not user-selectable: it is turned on by whichever indicator
	  needs it, and turning it on by hand buys a counter nothing reads.

	  WHERE THE COUNT HAPPENS, because this is the only thing about it that
	  could ever cost the radio anything: antr_on_message() runs on the
	  radiant API event thread - ordinary thread context, never a radio
	  callback - so the increment is free relative to the framing work
	  already being done per message. With the symbol off,
	  ant_activity_note_msg() is a macro expanding to nothing, so there is
	  no call and no argument evaluated.
